Package: credgate
Title: Detect Indian Personal Data Before It Reaches Language Models
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    c(person("Bharat", "Sikka", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
             email = "bharat8sikka@gmail.com"),
      person("Aishwarya", "Bais", role = c("aut", "cph"),
             email = "aishwarya.bais00@gmail.com"))
Description: Detects personal data in text before it is sent to a large
    language model, with Indian identifiers built in: Aadhaar (validated
    with the Verhoeff checksum), Aadhaar Virtual ID, PAN, GSTIN, voter ID,
    passport and driving licence numbers, UPI IDs, IFSC codes, bank account
    and payment card numbers, mobile numbers and Ayushman Bharat (ABHA)
    health IDs, plus rule-based detection of names and addresses in Latin
    and Indic scripts. Candidates are validated with checksums, scored from
    surrounding context and matched through Indic digits and invisible
    characters. The rules come from a language-neutral specification shared
    with the 'Python' package of the same name.
